From 525956489145d4e252ef81d7a1be3cbfcac4ec5b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VCKing101 <59761021+VCKing101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 09:29:28 +1030
Subject: [PATCH 26/53] Input: extra buttons, the controls a PSP lacks, for a
 port to use

A modern pad has L2, R2, L3 and R3; a PSP has none of them, so a game
never reads them, and the triggers only copied L and R. A port that wants
to give them a meaning of its own (a hint, a menu of the port's, a mode
switch) now can:

- GameProfile::extra_buttons names the ones the port uses (input::kExtraL2,
  kExtraR2, kExtraL3, kExtraR3). With L2 or R2 named, the analog triggers
  press L2 and R2 instead of copies of L and R, unless the player picked a
  trigger profile; with neither, nothing changes.
- hle_extension::extra_buttons() (interface version 5) gives the bits held
  when the game last read its pad. They are never written to the game's
  pad data.
- The keyboard binds them like any control: actions L2, R2, L3 and R3,
  input.bind.l2 and so on in settings.ini, listed in the menu only for the
  buttons the profile names. 1 and 3 are L2 and R2 by default (the number
  keys above Q and E, free in the default and the classic layouts); L3 and
  R3 have no key by default. The stick clicks are L3 and R3 on a pad.
- <prefix>_NO_EXTRA_BUTTONS=1 treats the profile's list as empty: the
  triggers press L and R again.

The input tests check the new defaults, that the keys press extra bits and
no PSP button, and the actions' bits.

Verified: the framework's 21 tests pass and portablekit_host_check builds
(Windows, MSVC); in the Dissidia 012 port, the keyboard's 1 and 3 and a
virtual pad's triggers reach the port as L2 and R2, and its loading screen
page did not see L or R from the triggers.
Not verified: other games, a real gamepad's triggers and stick clicks,
macOS and Linux builds.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
